#Ship Classes

; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Vasudan command installation — model supplied by the user.
; The original public Cairo table uses five BVas beams, three flak batteries,
; six AAAf beams, and heavy pulse turrets. This entry keeps that combat profile
; while using the uploaded HTL model and dedicated 6 km station beam profiles.
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
$Name: GVI Cairo
$Short name: VInst
$Species: Vasudan
+Tech Description:
XSTR("A large Vasudan command installation and fleet-production anchor. Its battery combines heavy anti-capital beams with layered anti-fighter defenses.", -1)
$end_multi_text
$POF file: htl_cairo.pof
$Detail distance: (0, 2000, 10000, 25000, 50000)
$Show damage: NO
$Collision Physics:
    +Bounce: 0.0
    +Both Small Bounce: 0.0
    +Rotation Factor: 0.0
    +Rotation Magnitude Maximum: 0.0
$Debris:
    +Damage Type: RTS Debris Impact
$Density: 1
$Damp: 0.2
$Rotdamp: 0.2
$Max Velocity: 0.0, 0.0, 0.0
$Rotation time: 200.0, 200.0, 200.0
$Rear Velocity: 0.0
$Forward accel: 0.0
$Forward decel: 0.0
$Slide accel: 0.0
$Slide decel: 0.0
$Expl inner rad: 100.0
$Expl outer rad: 2400.0
$Expl damage: 400.0
$Expl blast: 6500.0
$Expl Propagates: YES
; Death-roll rotation is separate from collision rotation; keep this station steady.
$Death Roll X rotation Cap: 0.0
$Death Roll Y rotation Cap: 0.0
$Death Roll Z rotation Cap: 0.0
$Shockwave Speed: 600.0
$Shockwave Count: 3
$Default PBanks: ()
$Default SBanks: ()
$SBank Capacity: ()
$Shields: 0
$Power Output: 1.0
$Max Oclk Speed: 0.0
$Max Weapon Eng: 100.0
$Hitpoints: 110000
$Armor Type: RTS Command Hull
$Shield Armor Type: RTS Command Hull
$Flags: ( "capital" "big damage" "in tech database" )
$AI Class: Captain
$Afterburner: NO
$Countermeasures: 0
$Scan time: 2000
$Closeup_pos: 0.0, 0.0, -2762
$Closeup_zoom: 0.5
$Score: 800
$Subsystem: Sensors, 5, 0
$Subsystem: Weapons, 5, 0
$Subsystem: Communications, 5, 0
